% If lines are still due, we ask of the next paragraph as many, with a 
% |\nobreak| between them, again unless that is over the limit.
% The next paragraph also writes its page, with what came so far; if that isn't 
% the page of the heading we warn, when the |.aux| is read at the end of the 
% run (|\@didactic@keep@after|), about the first such paragraph, since those 
% after it are on later pages too.
% That is the check on all of the above: what can end a page in such a gap, such 
% as the place to break before a list, is seen there.
